{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_clakuvc67e3zscfd5hsppnnuht3nb7ovdnuj2rnrzhz6icps4hiq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **The Rust translation is byte-identical to the C for all inputs — no divergence found.** The real bugs were in the *test harness*, and both are fixed.\n\n## Results\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` parity | ✅ 0 missing, 0 extra (default features: exact 1:1 on `get_predict_func`); 0 unresolved non-libc symbols |\n| Phase B — all 41 `CONFIGS.md` rows | ✅ pass across seeded randomized inputs |\n| Phase C — all 18 `ERRORS.md` rows | ✅ each has a passing differential test asserting the *exact* sentinel |\n| All feature × profile combos | ✅ `{none, difftest}` × `{debug, release}` — 4/4 |\n\n## Two harness bugs found and fixed\n\n1. **Stale `.so` was being verified.** `cargo test` does *not* rebuild a `cdylib`-only crate's `.so`, so the harness was `dlopen`-ing a leftover artifact. I proved this by mutating Rust's `_Pfn10` `>>3`→`>>4` — **all tests still passed**. The harness now always runs `cargo build --lib` itself into a private target dir (matching profile + features) and asserts the `.so` is newer than `src/lib.rs`. The same mutation now kills 6 tests.\n\n2. **A genuine coverage hole.** `mutation_coverage.py` (78 mutations) found one survivor: `BTAC1C2_GetPredictFunc`'s `default:` arm rerouted to `_Pfn0`. It's unobservable through the public API because `get_predict_func`'s own `default:` never inspects the returned pointer. Added `__difftest_selector` (reports *which* function was selected) and `__difftest_call_selected` (composed selector→predict pipeline) to both sides, plus rows C39–C41 / E8b–E8d. **Now 78/78 mutations killed.**\n\n## Key C quirks confirmed preserved (not \"fixed\")\n\n- `_Pfn10` uses `>>3` while generic `case 10` uses `>>4`\n- `_Pfn11` uses `>>1` while generic `case 11` uses `>>3`\n\nTests C32/C33 assert the two entry points *disagree identically* on both sides.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `c_src/` sources untouched. Internal `static` functions are reached via `translation/difftest_c/shim.c`, which `#include`s the original `lib.c` verbatim from outside the tree.\n- The `static` C functions correctly appear in **neither** `.so` — exporting them from Rust would itself be a divergence.\n- Coverage beyond the tables: struct-layout parity via `offsetof`, guard-page buffers proving `(idx-k)&7` never escapes the 8-element window, one-hot tap and one-hot `firfx` sweeps isolating every coefficient, and `i32::MIN`/`MAX` overflow-wrap checks.\n\nRun everything with `cd translation && ./run_verification.sh`; mutation check with `python3 mutation_coverage.py`. Both need `--offline` (crates.io is proxy-blocked here); `libloading 0.8.9` resolved from the local cargo cache."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":165145,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":915,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37c401f3-4722-4408-b0a7-032303b9d8b6","uuid":"2c988698-a11f-47aa-af3f-b2f46df478b3","timestamp":"2026-08-29T11:59:25.192Z"}
